WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.990
You li'l bastard!

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.490
You took a friendly swing at me

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.450
when I stopped you from 
making an ass of yourself.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.250
You weren't really trying to start 
a fight with me, now were you?

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.410
No...

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.380
Now, pay your bill and be on your way.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:58.300
Nothing to see here. Just a little horseplay.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.100
Sorry if we disturbed you.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.180
Thanks for all your help.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:05.990
It's nothing.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.600
You're a lifesaver.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.770
Oh, and here's what I owe you for 
last month. I'm sorry it's late.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.510
There's no need to apologize.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:14.570
I'm collecting interest on it.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.160
It doesn't have to be anything fancy,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.030
but could I get some sandwiches as payment?

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.290
Enough for two.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.970
"Duet by the Riverside"

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.090
This is legitimate self-defense.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.470
Giat was preparing for a coming war.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.780
They even had a mobile fortress in secret.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.560
Giat also had the Scrapped 
Princess in their possession,

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.560
and were even plotting to destroy the world.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:57.940
We must face Giat's act of 
invasion with the utmost resolve.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:02:59.990
But General,

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.450
we and Giat have maintained 
friendly relations for many years.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.310
It was Giat who attacked first.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.800
The Skid is destroyed,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.660
and there are no indications 
that they will attack again.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.130
I don't believe that there 
is any reason to fight.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.090
Are you trying to tell me 
to reverse my decision?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.130
I cannot send my unit to fight in such a war.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.890
Baroness, I am relieving you from the 
post of Special Forces Commander.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.350
Major Sturm.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.270
Sir.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.850
As of today, you are getting 
a two-rank promotion.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:35.110
The Special Forces will be 
under your command from now on.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.820
The death of the Scrapped Princess 
has yet to be confirmed.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.030
But depending on how it is used, the 
poison that will destroy the world

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.990
could also be used as a trump card 
to gain control of the world.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.040
First, we will use the entire army 
to capture the Scrapped Princess.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.210
Once we have the princess in our 
possession, this war is as good as won.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.680
Uh... I'm...

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.140
I'm home.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.520
Ow! That hurts! Cut it out!

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.480
You got an eyeful, didn't you?!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.440
Close the damn door!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.440
Moron! Watch what you're throwing!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.370
Of all the strays to pick up...

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.830
She's not dead.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.440
I'm positive that she's not dead.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.830
Even the Peacemakers are 
still looking for her.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:41.080
Rest a while. If you keep 
this up, you will collapse.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.010
If you wish to find your younger and 
older sisters before the Peacemakers do,

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.550
you should go about it in the 
most efficient manner possible.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.110
You and your efficiency!

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.890
Is that all you can say?!

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.560
If I drop from exhaustion,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.140
all you have to do is find somebody 
else with my genes, right?!

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:00.180
I do not... I never want 
to go through that again.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.390
If you do not wish to trust 
me, that is your choice.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.660
But let me tell you this.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:10.350
I stay at your side because I choose to.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.270
Not because of any duty or mission.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:16.670
I like to think that I myself 
chose to assist you.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.250
That is why I...

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.970
Pardon me!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.260
I'm sorry!

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.850
I need to eat something...

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.850
All the tables are full...

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.020
Hey, miss!

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.950
There's a seat open over here!

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.690
Mr. Berkens?

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.970
Well, I'll be! You're still alive!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.910
Are that old guy and the 
little lady with you?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.450
Well, uh...

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.140
Um, what are you doing here 
in the capital, Mr. Berkens?

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:00.360
I got called back by Church Headquarters.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.670
They said they lost track of the 
Scrapped Princess a couple weeks ago.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.640
After they dropped Ginnungagap 
on that mobile fortress,

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:09.430
the Royal Forces frantically searched 
for the Scrapped Princess' body,

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.680
but they didn't find anything.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:14.250
Right after that, information 
started going around

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:18.600
that a blonde-haired, blue-eyed girl had 
been spotted on the coast near Sauer.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.400
I don't know why, but they say that 
the Royal Forces have switched plans

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.270
from killing the Scrapped 
Princess to capturing her.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.360
Anyway, they shooed me out the door,

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.360
saying to find the Scrapped 
Princess right away.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:34.030
I know that you figured out who 
Pacifica really is, Mr. Berkens.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.830
No, it's not like that.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.750
I'm not interested in 
hauling in the little lady,

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.790
and I got fed up with eating country cooking.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.650
Wait a minute, are you by yourself?

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:48.760
Yes... I've been looking for the 
others for a long time now, though.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:50.520
The old guy, too?

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.390
Yes. I'm positive that they have to be 
alive, but there are so many people here,

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.060
and I don't even know where to begin looking.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.770
It's enough to make my head spin.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.520
Sounds like you're in a real bind.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:05.440
But now that I've run into you, 
I feel a little better somehow.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.190
It's like my father is at my side.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.250
Um. Right.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.010
Well, I'll tag along.

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.280
I don't have anything else to do.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:19.160
But if we don't find her before the 
Church or the Royal Forces do...

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.870
Relax, these things work themselves out.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.290
You really <i>are </i>like my father.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:29.760
Wow, an egg sandwich! It looks delicious!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.840
Don't get so worked up over 
a little thing like this.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.970
But we've been living on nothing 
but bread and cheese lately.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:37.720
Gee, sorry I don't bring in much money.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:38.930
Where'd you get these?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:40.980
Something happened at work.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.900
Oh, you want some tea? I'll put some on.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.810
Don't burn yourself again.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.190
No problem, no problem! Ow!

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:48.860
What did I just tell you, idiot?!

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:53.730
Hey...

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:58.100
Pamela isn't the name of 
your first love, is it?

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.950
It was the name of a cat 
I had a long time ago.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:01.710
A cat?!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.160
Oh, well.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.670
Wanna get going after we drink this?

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:08.340
Sure.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.750
Your troubles seem to be very deep, my son.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.840
If you like, you can tell me 
about it in the confessional.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.100
Admittedly, I'm still in training...

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:31.360
I appreciate the offer, but I'm 
not one of Mauser's faithful.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.060
That doesn't matter.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:39.540
What sort of priestess would I be if I 
turned a blind eye to a troubled man,

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.040
no matter who he is?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.040
The thing is, my older sister 
and little sister are missing.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:49.130
Oh, my... You must be worried sick.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.500
I've looked everywhere for them.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:55.680
I know they wouldn't have come here, 
but I figured it couldn't hurt.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.020
I'll pray for you.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.320
I'll pray that you find them soon.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.060
I'll have to make do with the sentiment.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.060
My little sister and I aren't really in 
a position to count on God's good graces.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.060
How long are you going to stay here?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.820
Have you converted or something?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.690
Is this your younger sister?

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:13.780
No, she isn't.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:17.150
She's a stranger who might've 
been my kid sister... once.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:22.130
The Church might change if it 
gets more priests like you.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.630
See you.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.960
Don't stay in there for too long, okay?

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.800
You're supposed to want to soak 
in the bath and relax, right?

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.700
You always keep me waiting for you.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.510
Go home without me, then.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:38.760
That's what I'll do, then.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.600
This is paradise...

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:48.100
Furet! I'm getting out!

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.020
Keep your voice down in here!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.480
You took forever!

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.920
My hair is cold now! And 
I just washed it, too!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:56.950
Sorry, sorry...

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.950
Oops. Oh, well, I'll drop 
it off next time we go.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.250
Hey, don't foist it off on me...

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.400
What's wrong, Pamela?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:22.390
I sometimes have these dreams 
where someone is chasing me.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:24.670
That someone's trying to kill me.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.100
Everybody has dreams like that.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.060
You really think so?

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.490
She's been stripped of her command?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:44.530
Apparently, the Baroness opposed the General.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.040
It sounds like Luke is going to 
be in charge of our unit, too.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.520
I wonder what's going on.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:54.880
We come to Bairach Manor time and again, 
and each time they say, "He isn't here."

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.090
Maybe I jumped to conclusions.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.720
In the letter Chris sent me,

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.890
he wrote, "The moon was beautiful 
that night in the glass valley,"

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:09.730
so I thought to myself, maybe Chris is 
looking up at the moon all alone right now.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.830
I'm sure he has a good reason.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.980
There was that big ruckus 
the other day, remember?

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.030
Things might be rough for this Chris person.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.820
After all, there might be a war soon.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:27.220
Plus, rumors are beginning to spread that 
the Scrapped Princess is in the capital.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:28.950
C'mon, let's buy this, too!

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.160
We don't need it.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.100
Aw, but we never have dessert!

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:33.540
I said, we don't need it.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.250
Tightwad.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.250
Pacifica...

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.080
Want me to buy it?

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:51.060
You want it, right?

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.610
What, really?!

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.320
I got a little money yesterday.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:55.900
Gosh, I don't know!

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.860
Do I look funny?

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.820
No, and yes...

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:05.820
What's <i>that </i>mean?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.370
More importantly, are you 
gonna make it to your job?

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.750
Oh, no! I almost forgot!

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:17.920
Leo?

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:26.510
What is it?

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.220
It's nothing.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.900
If you're enchanted by my beauty, 
don't hold back on my account.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:33.980
I'm impressed that you've 
become so self-conscious.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.070
What's <i>that </i>mean?

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:38.020
Why don't <i>you </i>do something about 
those old fart tendencies of yours?

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.190
Well, I'll see you later. Take this, okay?

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.360
As you wish, Highness.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:43.820
See ya!

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:49.450
Step right up. There's laughter, there's 
tears, and there's romance inside.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.370
See the play and pay as you leave,

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.410
Keydarf!

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:55.960
Oh, my! You almost look like 
a respectable young lady!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.840
So I'm not always a respectable young lady?

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.720
Uh... C'mon, the play's about 
to start. Go on and get ready.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.940
Okay!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:10.800
Oh, my.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.640
Would you cut it out and get lost?

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:20.070
You have no choice in the matter.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.190
As long as the Providence Breaker's 
death remains unconfirmed,

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:25.910
we will assume that she is still alive.

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:30.280
Because your sister possesses 
the ability to elude our scans,

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.240
all I can do is accompany you and observe.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.460
If she can't be detected by you people,

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.870
maybe it's for the best that 
I can't find her, either.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:41.520
I should warn you, Steyr's 
pronouncement remains in effect.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:45.250
Unless you present hard evidence that the 
Providence Breaker is in the capital,

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.930
we will kill 10,000 for each day that passes.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.850
I'm looking for her as hard as I can, too!

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.680
I've had about enough of your crap!

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:54.520
If you're weapons, I wish 
you'd <i>look </i>like weapons.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.450
That goes for Zefiris and Natalie, too.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.400
You go around in human form 
and act like you're humans,

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:04.940
but then you say heartless, inhuman 
things as if it were nothing.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:08.150
I'll admit that from your point 
of view, we are the enemy,

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:11.700
and are merciless, evil beings.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:16.370
But we have always been the caretakers 
of this world, and of the human race.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:18.590
Caretakers of the human race, huh?

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.330
Even if it means killing countless people.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:25.360
If it is for the greater good, 
then yes, without hesitation.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.660
She really is dead, isn't she?

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:28.800
Cin, I mean.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.760
You monster.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.310
She's lost her memory?!

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.250
She goes by the name "Pamela" now.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.520
Furet gave it to her, apparently.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:45.280
Furet? Is that the man who was with her?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.650
He helped her out, and has been 
letting her stay at his place.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:53.160
W-W-What? You mean to say that 
he and Miss Pacifica are...

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:53.790
Living together?

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:54.740
Are living together?!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:58.450
I bumped into the little lady 
in the street by chance, too.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:01.000
Oh, I quit my old assassin gig.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.580
I'm working as a musician here now.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.000
An assassin?!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.760
When we first met, Mr. Keydarf 
here tried to kill Miss Pacifica.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:08.880
Wait a minute...

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:11.970
Do you know, too? Do you 
know that Pacifica is...

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.200
Huh? You know, too, Miss Winia?

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.720
I had no idea that you knew...

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:19.220
I don't think it's a good idea for her to 
be wandering the streets of the capital,

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:24.560
but I don't have the heart to tell 
her that she's the Scrapped Princess.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:27.690
I asked the playhouse owner 
if she could work here.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:30.070
Thank you for going to all this trouble.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:32.660
Anyway, I'm having her play a horse.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.900
That way, no one can tell who she is.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.580
I understand. Please hire me, as well.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.120
Leo?

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.620
I even have my own costume!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.260
Hold it right there!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.280
Foul dragon of the devil!

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.040
I shall smite thee in Mauser's stead!

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.810
You sure get into your role.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:03.600
Who is that?

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:05.850
A youngster who wants to be a comedian.

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:07.740
He begged me to hire him.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:11.190
Oh, and I hired a new concessions girl, too.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.030
I get the feeling that 
we're gonna hit it off!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.490
I'm Pamela!

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:17.980
Nice to meet you!

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.750
I'm Winia. It's nice to meet you.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.490
Wow, they really liked you out there!

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:28.750
I bet you're gonna make a great jester, um...

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:29.420
I'm Leo.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.380
Nice to meet you, Leo!

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.840
Good show, everybody!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.230
Good show today.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:38.810
See you again tomorrow, okay?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.430
For now, I think we should 
leave her be, don't you?

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:48.230
She might be better off like this.

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:52.190
Maybe the old her would want it this way.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:57.030
If you like, you two can 
stay at the playhouse.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.450
Thank you.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.120
And here you go!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.330
How was work today?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.790
You didn't break any dishes, did you?

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.370
No.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:07.040
You come home with cuts sometimes.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.750
You sure are a klutz, Furet!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.800
Washing dishes can be dangerous, you know.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.960
Y'know, Furet, you sure 
seem mature for your age.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.770
Are you really 18?

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:18.760
I was in the army for a while.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:22.080
Oh, you're an ex-soldier, 
huh? At your age, too.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:24.180
I was only in the army for three years.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:32.660
What's this for?

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:33.740
To say thanks.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.280
You bought me this dress,

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.200
and you're letting me mooch off of you.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.030
I can't do anything for you for myself, so...

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:42.990
Thanks for putting up with someone like me.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:44.910
I guess you're right.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.790
You're a terrible cook, you only smear 
the dirt in circles when you clean,

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.460
and you burn yourself when you make tea.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.420
You don't have to spell it out like that!

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.480
You were the one who said it, not me.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:18:00.550
Oh, wow! They're lined up 
side by side! That's so cute!

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:01.930
Just eat them, okay?

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:03.470
Welcome, have a seat!

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:05.770
I bet you're starving.

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:08.020
Order whatever you want.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:11.940
Pacifica?!

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.940
Miss Raquel?

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:16.520
Who's that?

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.410
You got split up while you were on a trip?

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:21.700
Yes.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.660
The ship we were aboard was wrecked, 
and we were thrown into the sea.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:26.820
Oh, I see.

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:30.380
I hear that there were a lot of shipwrecks 
because of that Ginnungagap spell.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.300
Still, this is great, isn't it? 
You've found your sister and father.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.670
"Father"?! Um, right.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.220
Thank you for looking after my daughter.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.760
Oh. Um, we haven't done 
anything... inappropriate.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.470
I should hope not!

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:45.140
Who are you?

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.720
Miss Pacifica's betrothed!

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.060
Something like that...

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.730
So let's go, shall we?

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:57.040
I guess this is goodbye, 
Pamela. I mean Pacifica.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:57.690
Goodbye?

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.160
Well, because you've found your family.

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:04.500
I don't want to go.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:07.510
You show up out of the blue and 
say you're my parents or whatever,

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:09.330
but I don't remember anything.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.120
Pamela...

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.150
I don't want to go.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:13.850
I want to stay here.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.090
I can't stay anymore?

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:25.100
Um...

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.620
If it's all right, would you 
let her stay here for a while?

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:29.930
Hey!

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:32.810
We were thrown overboard with nothing 
but the clothes on our backs,

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.900
and we're living in an inn at the moment.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:36.900
It would only be for a while.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.900
Just until we can contact my little brother, 
who ought to be here in the capital.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.860
But...

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.360
Please, I beg you.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.830
Well, I... I don't really care.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.290
We'll drop by from time to time, okay?

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.210
Okay...

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:59.080
T-Take good care of my daughter.

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:01.810
Are you sure about this?

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:06.010
Well, it seems like forever since 
the last time I saw her so relaxed.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:09.080
We've been hounded ever 
since we left our village.

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:14.690
Besides, if things stay like 
this and her birthday comes

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.330
without anyone knowing she's 
the Scrapped Princess...

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.010
Furet? Are you asleep?

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:29.200
No.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:33.710
Should I have left?

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.720
It doesn't really matter.

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:36.830
You're like a stray cat 
that I found on the street.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.170
You're mean.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:42.110
Pamela?

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.600
It's nice here.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.380
The sound of the river, I mean.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.390
It sends me right to sleep.

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:54.500
Good night, Furet.

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:57.300
Good night, Pamela.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:36.540
The Cassul siblings have been 
separated in the capital.

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:39.040
Shannon keeps trying his 
hardest to find the others.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.200
Raquel has found their little sister first,

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:43.670
but Pacifica keeps avoiding her.

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:45.630
Pacifica has gotten the normal 
life she's always wanted,

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:47.280
but will she be able to keep it?

00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:48.640
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:49.680
"A Chanson for Fleeting Moments."

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
